# Example vi: an industrial welding arm uses a vendor extension when it has one.
# Cleaned up from spec-source/URITP - Google Docs.pdf, following spec/DECISIONS.md:
#   A2  5mms became 5mm/s
#   A12 the seam is route.seam and its start is places.seam_start
# "examplecorp" is the made-up vendor name the Guidebook uses for extensions.

robot welder = connect("line3:examplecorp-x7")
move welder.tool to places.seam_start
if welder.has("examplecorp.adaptive_weld"):
    examplecorp.adaptive_weld(route.seam, current=180A)
else:
    weld along route.seam speed 5mm/s current 180A
move welder.tool to places.home
